<mei xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei" meiversion="5.0"><meiHead xml:lang="en"><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Pa 1871-64v-1</title></titleStmt><pubStmt><identifier>https://corpus-monodicum.de/d/70ac8650-1a9f-41ce-a987-96e1265a2f46</identifier><respStmt><corpName role="publisher">Corpus Monodicum</corpName></respStmt><address><addrLine>Domerschulstraße 13</addrLine><addrLine>97070 Würzburg</addrLine></address><availability><useRestrict auth.uri="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</useRestrict></availability><date isodate="2026-11-04"/></pubStmt><seriesStmt><title>Corpus Monodicum</title><respStmt><resp>Edition (Ordinariumsgesänge)</resp><persName>Andreas Pfisterer</persName></respStmt><funder>Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz</funder></seriesStmt><notesStmt><annot startid="#m-89b66001-8d2c-44ea-9e7c-9f3fa1560937" endid="#m-d214df1c-3e15-439a-8220-3fc156f1033a"><table><tr><td><rend>((dextram))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>korrigiert aus ((dexteram)), regulär notiert.</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-4b23cb49-f1f3-4903-8113-ee0cc387b760" endid="#m-8343b764-07ed-4024-a79f-35cf424a4dc3" type="emendation"><table><tr><td><rend>((polus)) (wie ((CT XII)))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>((polum))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-cbbaa2cd-a1b8-486a-b5d0-1f71bf47db10" endid="#m-8d5dd1ba-5df1-43bf-85f6-952b665ae983"><table><tr><td><rend>((seduli))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>korrigiert aus ((sedule))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-b2819535-00c0-4a9d-9be2-b135e802bd25" endid="#m-5f5d21e6-781f-43b1-b1ae-d8e62948e8e0"><table><tr><td><rend>((pacis))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>semantisch plausibler: ((patris)) (wie ((CT XII))).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-b141da70-e4e3-4d9f-b0cd-db88254c4f00" endid="#m-bc189bce-48d7-4944-8549-9270b4599eca"><table><tr><td><rend>((Vota ... exaudi))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>Das ganze Element bildet eine Variante zu dem in ((Pa 1118)) überlieferten ((Atque uoto humillimi sedulis libenter exaudi adonai)). Dies lässt sich mit kleinen Emendationen zu einem verständlichen Text machen: ((Atque uota humillimi seduli libenter exaudi adonai)) (vgl. ((CT XII))). Das der Melodie wegen nicht emendierbare ((sublimii)) in ((Pa 1871)) entzieht sich dem Verständnis.</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-fb13e0be-510d-4f0e-bf5e-360a130dbb28" endid="#m-deeb56d2-5690-4b95-ac1d-53474e8c9200"><table><tr><td><rend>((quem))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>korrigiert aus ((que))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-ecb996b9-8e63-486c-9ed9-dfad65450f1a" endid="#m-8c601bca-3810-468e-998b-6a65666c2e04"><table><tr><td><rend>((par manentem))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>semantisch plausibler: ((permanentem)) (wie ((CT XII))).</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-c1c6c2d3-145d-4c50-a541-c1a1af67d48e" endid="#m-c5548bee-d119-4cba-9c0c-ae3d32cf1fb8" type="emendation"><table><tr><td><rend>((pater)) (wie ((CT XII)))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>((patri))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-57221f86-ad82-4a48-b458-a413f80fff32" endid="#m-4b41152d-7658-43bb-9c71-608c03b554c7" type="emendation"><table><tr><td><rend>((Altitonans)) (wie ((CT XII)))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>((Altitonant))</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot startid="#m-40a24a8b-71ba-4dc0-9b45-57d7d4f2bf2b" endid="#m-fa8e1459-8df7-4868-a624-2fd2e0fe5895"><table><tr><td><rend>((†Semper ... almis†))</rend></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>Der ohne Varianten in drei Handschriften (((Pa 1118, Pa 1871, MaA 51))) überlieferte Text bleibt unverständlich. Wenn die nahe liegende Gliederung in vier 5p-Verse mit einsilbigem Reim bleiben soll, ist wenig Raum für Emendationen.</rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot type="global-comment"><table><tr><td><rend>((1-5, 6-9:)) Hexameter.</rend></td></tr></table></annot></notesStmt><sourceDesc><source xml:id="wit-pa-1871"><bibl><identifier type="siglum">Pa 1871</identifier></bibl></source></sourceDesc></fileDesc><encodingDesc><appInfo><application version="0.9.1"><name>Monodi-Zero</name></application></appInfo></encodingDesc><workList><work><identifier>Pa 1871-64v-1</identifier><title>Quem patris ad dextram</title><incip><incipText><p>Quem patris ad dextram</p></incipText></incip><contents><contentItem><locus from="64v">f. 64v, l. 1</locus></contentItem></contents><biblList><bibl>CT XII, 75: 1 2 3 4 5 11 12 13 16 14 15 6 7 8 9</bibl></biblList><classification><termList><term type="genre">Gloria</term><term type="genre">tropiert</term><term type="feast">Messe</term><term type="Editor">Andreas Pfisterer</term><term type="Endseite">64v</term><term type="Endzeile">13</term><term type="Melodiennummer_Katalog">Bosse 51</term><term type="Cantus_ID">509502</term><term type="Band_Genre">Ordinariumsgesänge</term></termList></classification></work></workList><manifestationList><manifestation><identifier type="siglum">Pa 1871</identifier><identifier type="cantus">Pa 1871</identifier><titleStmt><title>Pa 1871</title></titleStmt><creation><geogName role="origin">Moissac</geogName><geogName role="origin-region">Quellen aquitanischer Herkunft</geogName><corpName role="origin-institution">Abtei Saint-Pierre</corpName><date>11. Jh 2. Hälfte</date></creation><langUsage><language xml:lang="la"/></langUsage><classification><termList><term type="quellentyp">Tropar, Sequentiar, Prosar, Prosular</term></termList></classification><itemList><item><identifier type="shelfmark">Nouv. acq. lat. 1871</identifier><physLoc><repository><geogName role="settlement">Paris</geogName><corpName>Bibliothèque nationale de France</corpName></repository></physLoc></item></itemList><relationList><relation rel="hasReproduction" target="https://gallica.bnf.fr/iiif/ark:/12148/btv1b85624659/manifest.json" label="IIIF manifest"/></relati